From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:20:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ps: VerifyRsaSha256

The BOSS module (LLE) checks the signatures in downloaded SpotPass files
with ps:ps VerifyRsaSha256 (e.g. Miitopia's Mii Central MiiTube.dat and
questionnaire). The call was unimplemented; the "success" it returned
only came from the generic unimplemented-function reply.

VerifyRsaSha256 now really checks the RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 SHA-256
signature with the modulus and exponent from the RSA context buffer and
logs the outcome, then reports success either way: files from a custom
SpotPass server (edited or new content) can't carry Nintendo's
signature and must still be accepted. Test with a generated key.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
